Check-in rule (applies when the input says a check-in was sent):
- The assistant already checked in after the customer went quiet: it asked whether they need anything else, repeated an earlier question, or offered email follow-up from the team.
- When the assistant's latest message is a check-in the customer didn't answer, the conversation is COMPLETE unless an earlier customer request is still unanswered. This overrides the rule about questions or information the customer hasn't provided.
- An unanswered lead follow-up offer or follow-up form is not an unmet request.
